  "narration": {
    "title": "Misiorowski Holds a Pinned Needle in Milwaukee",
    "intro": "It's a pitching day, and the contenders are leaning on their arms. Milwaukee runs the rotation board, the Braves run the bullpen board, and one young Brewer is still untouchable.",
    "staff_lead": "Milwaukee tops the starter-ERA ranking at 3.19, just ahead of the Dodgers (3.27) and Rays (3.29) \u2014 three of the league's best teams, all built on the mound. The Yankees (3.38) and Tigers (3.66) fill out the top five.",
    "bullpen_lead": "Atlanta owns the reliever-ERA board at 2.77, the clear standout, with the Yankees (3.18) and Red Sox (3.20) trailing. A deep Braves bullpen is doing quiet work even as the team slid in the power ranking.",
    "arms_lead": "Jacob Misiorowski leads the elite arms with a form pinned at 100, a 1.45 ERA and a 0.77 WHIP, and he's holding it steady. Cam Schlittler is right behind at 94 with a 1.62 ERA for the Yankees; further down, Chris Sale's 2.10 mark anchors the Braves.",
    "risers_lead": "Eduardo Rodriguez climbed five points of form to 76, matched by Logan Webb's five-point bump to 72. Max Meyer added four to reach 75 \u2014 small steps, but all heading the right way."
  }
